WHEREAS, the Board of Public Utilities (Board)is authorized by State Statute and City Code to set
rates, fees and penalties for water and sanitary sewer services furnished to customers; and
(a)Pay for the operation and maintenance of the sanitary sewer system, including salaries,
wages and benefits, and the cost of all materials and supplies necessary for repairs,
replacements and upgrades to the system;
(b)Pay interest charges and principal payments on all outstanding sewer loans and bonds as
they are due;
(c) Cover all miscellaneous expenses;
(d) Cover all usual extensions and enlargements, together with a reasonable allowance for
(e)Provide and maintain a depreciation fund for the sewer department;
WHEREAS, the Board has determined that an increase in the sewer rates is necessary to ensure
adequate revenue is generatedin order topayfor costs associated with those services;
WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the Cityof Cheyenne, pursuant to Ordinance3894, adopted June
14, 2010, requires that prior to the beginning of each fiscalyear, the Board will calculate new Sewer rates,
service charges, penalties and miscellaneous charges based on the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price
Index, All Urban Consumers, Water and Sewer Maintenance and the Wyoming Cost of Living Index -
Southeast Region andpreparea new Sewerfee schedule;
WHEREAS, the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index, All Urban Consumers, Water and
Sewer Maintenance for the calendar year 2012was 6.7% and the Wyoming Cost of Living Index-Southeast
Region for the fourth quarter of 2012 was 3.4%; and
WHEREAS, the Board has determined that an additional sewer rate increase of $.05per1,000gallons is
necessary topay for the annual principal and interest charges on a loan for future infrastructure improvements
related to Southern Sewer Collection Project Phase I.
NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that the sewerrate schedule will be adjusted by the Wyoming
Cost Living Index -Southeast Region for the fourth quarter of 2012 of 3.4% and by $.05 per 1,000 gallons.
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the following Sewer Rate Schedule is adopted by the Board, and
that it be presented in theform of an ordinance to the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne forapproval, to
become effective on consumption and bills issued on or after the dates notedbelow on the Sewer rate schedule:
