WHEREAS, the Board of Public Utilities ("BOARD")has exclusive authority to manage,
operate, maintain and control the Cheyenne Municipal Waterworks, Sanitary Sewage System and
Water Reclamation Facilities of the City and to make all rules and regulations necessary for the
safe, economical and efficient operation and maintenance of the above facilities; and
WHEREAS, the Board has determined that an increase in the fees is necessary to pay for
costs associated with: the new connectors share of systems; water and sewer development; water
and sewer debt service; over-sizing certain water and sewer mains; and the expansionto thewater
and sewer systems; and
WHEREAS, the BOARD desires to set the fees to secure anincome sufficient to:
(a)Pay for costs associated with the tap installations;
(b）Recover costs and to reduce debt associated with water and sewer development
and expansion for new connectors tothe City'swater and sewersystem;
(c)Pay for costs associated with the water and sewer over-sizing and extensions; and
WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne, pursuant to Ordinance 3895,
adopted June 14, 2010, requires that prior to the beginning of each fiscal year, the Board will
calculate new tap fees, system development fees, pump stationfees, and other related fees based
on the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index, All Urban Consumers, Water and
Sewer Maintenance and the Wyoming Cost of Living Index-Southeast Region and prepare new
tap fees, system development fees, pump station fees and other related fee schedules; and
WHEREAS, the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index, All Urban
Consumers, Water and Sewer Maintenance for the calendar year 2012 was 6.7% and the
Wyoming Cost of Living Index-Southeast Region for the fourth quarter of 2012was 3.4%.
