DUMP AND COMMERCIAL WASTE RATES TO BE CHARGED TO
USERS OF THE CHEYENNE WATER AND SEWER SYSTEM"
WHEREAS, the Board of Public Utilities (Board)is authorized by State Statute and City Code to
set rates, fees and penalties for water and sanitary sewer services furnished to customers; and
(a)Pay for the operation and maintenance of the sanitary sewer system, including
salaries, wages and benefits, and the cost of all materials and supplies necessary for
repairs, replacements and upgrades to the system;
(b)Pay interest charges and principal payments on all outstanding sewer loans and bonds
as they are due;
(c) Cover all miscellaneous expenses;
(d) Cover all usual extensions and enlargements, together with a reasonable allowance
for emergency and unforeseen expenses; and
(e)Provide and maintain a depreciation fund for the sewer department;
WHEREAS, the Board has determined that an increase in the Septic Waste Dump and
Commercial Waste rates are necessary to ensure adequate revenue is generated in order to payfor costs
associated with those services rendered;
WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne, pursuant to Ordinance3896, adopted
June14,2010, requires that prior to the beginningof each fiscal year, the Board will calculate new septic
waste dump rates and commercial waste rates based on the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price
Index, All Urban Consumers, Water and Sewer Maintenance and the Wyoming Cost Living Index -
Southeast Region and prepare a new septic waste dump rates and commercial waste rates schedule; and
WHEREAS, the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index, All Urban Consumers, Water
and Sewer Maintenance for the calendar year 2012was 6.7% and the Wyoming Cost of Living Index --
Southeast Region for the fourth quarter of 2012was 3.4%.
NOW THERFOREBE IT RESOLVED that the septicwaste dump and commercial waste rate
schedule will be adjusted by the Wyoming Cost of Living Index-Southeast Region for thefourth quarter
of 2012 of 3.4%.
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the following Rate Schedule for septic waste dump and
commercial wasteis adoptedby the Board, and that it be presented in the form of an ordinance to the
Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne for approval, and will become effective on statements rendered,
tickets purchased, and on septic and commercial waste delivered on or after January 1, 2014:
